  "note": "Phoenix / Scottsdale / Valley of the Sun, Arizona joined as the THIRTY-SEVENTH market and the first Arizona market at 256 published pet-friendly profiles over 18 publishing corridors (downtown-phoenix, biltmore-camelback-arcadia, phx-sky-harbor, tempe, old-town-scottsdale, central-scottsdale, paradise-valley, mesa, chandler, glendale, scottsdale-airpark-kierland, north-scottsdale, north-phoenix-deer-valley, west-phoenix, gilbert, goodyear-avondale-litchfield, surprise-sun-city, buckeye), on package pkg-phoenix-az-07f7e75699af6a8c. Built from zero on the Denver-live lineage, registered as COMPOSITE_FRESH_MARKET_DATA_ONLY with 0 broad regression runs, corrected before authorization (four Wyndham vacation-ownership resorts moved to TIMESHARE, outside hotel inventory), and founder-authorized once (PTF-PHOENIX-AZ-FOUNDER-LAUNCH-AUTHORIZATION-004; the earlier packages pkg-phoenix-az-85ad9b66 and pkg-phoenix-az-865822f4 were refused) -- this market's FIRST authorization and FIRST deployment, so nothing was superseded. The exact authorized artifact was deployed with no rebuild: the served sitemap hashes to the authorized candidate, the served route SET is identical to it, all 3343 parent routes refetched 200 with 0 lost, all 276 Phoenix routes are live, and every unpublished census row returns 404 -- 48 Places-gated, 30 founder-decision rows (fourteen dual-brand buildings and two redirect-domain rulings, no identity_resolutions.json ruling written), 88 router-exhausted / evidence / source-silent, three hotels not yet open and the 59 verified-no-pets rows, which publish only as exclusions. Sedona, Flagstaff, the Grand Canyon, Prescott and Tucson remain refused. The other 8 corridors stay below their own publication minimum and were not forced. Rollback is the deployment Phoenix replaced (Denver-live, 36 markets).",
